                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "NightCry is a pretty bad point and click, horror game and what makes it even more sad is that it’s done by some of the original team that worked on the original Clock Tower games, but what is the story.\n\nOn a cruise ship people are having a good time, whatever it’s on their honeymoon, attending a fancy party or for business. But unbeknownst to these passengers especially three passengers, one of them a young girl named Rooney, a creature with a giant pair of scissors soon attacks everyone. Now we follow the story of three people desperately trying to escape, will they or will they go down to Davy Jones locker.\n\nOkay the likes, the gameplay is a mixed bag I'll talk more about it in the dislikes, but the basis is like Clock Tower and Clock Tower 2, the monster shows up and you must run, hide or find different items that could be used as a weapon to chase the creature off, nothing too complicated, but again it does have a big problem. The puzzles are okay some of them are actually were pretty clever like the suitcase puzzle and the billiard puzzle.\n\nThe graphics are okay it has a nice use of colors and designs, they remind me of the graphics from Deadly Premonition which is not a bad thing, the graphics in that game were good. The levels are good I mean the idea of a Scissorman like stalker attacking a ship is an interesting idea and the ship does feel like a real cruise ship with cabins, a mini bar, dance floor that sort of thing, it was nice to look at it and explore.\n\nThe music was okay nothing really to write home about, did have some nice music for the chase sequence when being hunted by the stalker. The stalker Scissor walker is okay for a Scissorman like character it has a creepy design the way it moves and snaps its giant scissors.\n\nThe atmosphere is okay nothing that really keeps you on your toes; honestly I blame it with the terrible control that really affects the atmosphere. Now is this game scary not really there is nothing that makes you jump out or scare you, it does have some unique kills and some pretty disturbing imagery, but other than that not scary at all.\n\nOkay the dislikes, the gameplay is pretty damn bad mostly it's the controllers like it’s really bad to the point where you'll be fighting more of the controls then the actual stalker, you see in normal point and click games all you have to do is click or double click to make the character walk or run to this place.\n\nThe problem is that it’s so hard to control the character even when clicking they can go in different directions or they legitimately run into the stalker or they just take their sweet time walking, even when clicking it multiple times, even when they're being chased by the stalker.\n\nAlso the stamina I don't know I feel like the stamina runs out way too quickly and it takes way too long for your character to get its stamina back, there are also branching paths in this game, but because the controls are so bad I couldn't even be bothered to explore those paths, especially since there are no achievements for doing it.\n\nThe story is also really confusing and leaves a lot of unanswered questions, like why is the villain of this game doing all this, where did the scissor man like character come from and why are they supernatural. I mean the game does kind of explain it somewhat, but it's still very confusing.\n\nAlso why is the main character Rooney connected to a death of a girl, what is that about? There is probably a better explanation in one of the branching paths, but again because of the bad gameplay I couldn't even be bothered to find the different paths.\n\nThe voice acting is pretty bad, I mean no offense to the actors and actresses but it feels like they're barely giving a performance like this was a simple paycheck, which I can understand they probably weren't paid a lot, but still they could have at least had some fun with it, like there are some voice actors who even if the game is kind of bad they still give a pretty good performance and raise the game to a solid B.\n\nThe characters were all so bad they were either jackasses or idiots or both. Like sometimes when reading the dialogue I was like, oh my God you are an asshole is this now the right time to be a petty dickwad or picking on someone when there's a giant monster running about.\n\nNow the worst part of Nightcry is the fact that this game was kickstarted, thankfully I'm not one of the original kickstarters but whoever Kickstarted this game expecting it to be like a modern Clock Tower game I feel very, very bad for them.\n\nLike I said there are a lot of other Clock Tower inspired games either by triple A studios or Indie developers that feel like a better love letter/Clock Tower inspired game like the remothered series, some mascots horror games and Bye Sweet Carole and just so many others that do this formula far, far better.\n\nSo with done, NightCry is a pretty bad point and click, horror game and what makes it even more sad is that it’s done by some of the original team that worked on the original Clock Tower games, normally here I talk about what's really to like about the game, before following up with a recommendation but I can't recommend this game. \n\nIt does have some interesting ideas, but due to the terrible gameplay, confusing story and just unlikable characters I can't recommend this game, it's just so bad and they're just so many other Clock Tower inspired games that are way better than this, hell there's the newly ported Clock Tower the first fear by WayForward that is worth your time and money. I mean you want to get this game okay I would say wait till it's on sale but I don't think it's ever been on sale.",
